        "Claude Code 2.1.314",
        "Claude Code v2.1.314 can refuse file edits outside your working directories in every permission mode.",
        "This release tightens the boundaries around file edits: one setting makes Write, Edit and NotebookEdit reject any path outside your working directories, whatever permission mode is active. On long sessions, VS Code and Claude Desktop now summarize an idle conversation above 200K tokens and reuse that summary on your next message when the prompt cache has expired. The rest is a long list of fixes aimed at sessions that failed turn after turn, including effort caps set by an admin, oversized image histories on Bedrock, and gateways rejecting beta headers or tool search blocks.",
        "A new permission setting fences edits to your working directories in every mode, and idle compaction on the Code tab now reaches more setups: subscribers with telemetry disabled, plus Bedrock, Vertex, Foundry and LLM gateways, but in those last cases only after the one-hour prompt cache is enabled.",
        "You can keep a session from touching files outside the project without switching permission modes by hand. Long conversations stop losing context after a pause, and failures that used to end silently now surface: claude -p reports the startup error instead of finishing with exit code 0 and nothing printed.",
        "For developers running Claude Code in headless and CI jobs, on Bedrock or Vertex through a gateway, and anyone who leaves long sessions open in the Code tab.",
        "Writes fenced to working dirs",
