        "GitHub Copilot app security extension: triage and fix code scanning alerts in preview",
        "The security extension pulls your open code scanning alerts into the app, sorted by severity, with search and filters. Pick one or more and have Copilot explain or fix them. Edits stay in your local working copy, so you review and push when ready. Linked pull requests show whether a fix is already under way, and dismissals routed through delegated alert dismissal go for approval. Run /security-review on current changes to see new findings alongside existing alerts, and the extension flags when the code has moved since the last review. You can also ask about alerts in chat.",
        "Alert triage and fixes no longer require jumping between github.com and the editor; the extension keeps the alert list, its details and the affected code in one place.",
        "Browse open alerts by severity, filter the list, read details with the affected code, then hand a batch to Copilot for an explanation or a local fix you can iterate on.",
