        "Claude Code 2.1.317",
        "Claude Code v2.1.317: guardrails on scheduled tasks that pick up connectors you did not ask for",
        "This release tightens a few places where an action could go further than you intended. Scheduled tasks now warn you when they pick up connectors you never asked for, and a web or shell tool call that would send your account email to the network stops for a check first. Agent SDK hook callbacks get an onFailure: \"block\" option, so a failing callback stops the action rather than letting it through. If you run Claude Code on your own hardware or through a gateway, there are fixes here too: runner sessions reconnect instead of reusing a dead connection after server errors, and claude -p no longer exits 0 when a full disk or quota ate its transcript.",
        "Three additions stand out for anyone automating Claude Code. Scheduled cloud tasks surface unexpected connector additions with instructions for removing them, outbound email leaks get a confirmation prompt, and hook authors can now make a failure block the action. Admin APIs also grew a cost report for past spend.",
        "You can see what a scheduled task attached to itself before it runs, keep your email out of tool calls unless you say yes, and let a broken hook stop work instead of failing silently. Self-hosted runner sessions recover better after server errors, and a disk-full run now reports failure instead of exiting successfully.",
        "Teams running Claude Code on self-hosted runners or through a gateway, hook authors on the Agent SDK, and anyone administrating cloud scheduled tasks and spend reporting.",
