        "A Closer Look at Phonon TTS. Launching High-Quality On-Device Speech That Tops the Benchmarks.",
        "Phonon from Gradium puts speech on your own device, with the weights open.",
        "Gradium launched Phonon, a small text-to-speech model that needs no server and no network, so what you type stays local. Phonon 31m is Apache 2.0 and can go into commercial products; the 40m model covers all five languages non-commercially, and commercial use of those is priced by user count according to the publisher. Custom voices come from cloning or plain-text design in Gradium Studio. A Transformers path handles batch work, while ptts runs a single stream on device across many backends.",
        "The model descends from Pocket TTS and produces audio through flow matching, a different approach from what other speech systems use. The team credits that choice for packing this quality into a small footprint, though it made training tricky at the start.",
        "Get speech out of phones, laptops, single-board computers and browser tabs with no round trip to a server, and keep phone numbers, dates and codes readable.",
        "Only Phonon 31m is Apache 2.0; the other models are CC BY-NC and cost money for commercial use, priced by user count.",
