        "Higgsfield Shorts builds 9:16 videos hosted by an AI presenter that may return across a series",
        "You upload the character, product or clothing you want on screen — up to 38 images or videos — and the presenter speaks a script written for the short. A reference clip is optional: give it 10 to 120 seconds of footage and its motion carries over onto your character. Pick a length (15 seconds, 30 seconds, 1 minute or 2 minutes) and Basic or High quality, then generate on the site or from Claude through Higgsfield MCP. The point is a series, not a one-off: the same face and voice can come back episode after episode, which is what a brand needs if it posts weekly.",
        "This is the launch of Shorts itself: a vertical short-form generator built around an AI host rather than around a single clip. Inputs are split into character, script and an optional motion reference, and existing AI Influencer characters or earlier generations can be reused straight from the account.",
        "You get a host who walks through a product, wears a piece of clothing or rides a trend, and the same character can anchor a whole run of episodes. Voice is picked separately — male, female or custom — or auto-generated to match the uploaded character. Motion from a popular clip can be replayed on your own presenter.",
