        "Mistral Large 4 lands on Hugging Face with open weights",
        "Le Chonk is a sparse mixture-of-experts model from Mistral that reads text and images and writes text back, with roughly 1T total and 49B active parameters and room for a 1M-token context. It arrives in FP8 and NVFP4 builds, and Unsloth and the llama.cpp team also publish GGUFs. transformers, vLLM and llama.cpp get support on release day, and TRL handles fine-tuning. Mistral points it at cybersecurity and coding agents, and because the weights are open, you decide the usage policy and where it runs.",
        "Two kinds of sparsity in one model: the language model routes each token to a handful of experts, and a DeepSeek Sparse Attention indexer picks which earlier positions to attend to. A Pixtral vision encoder handles images, and a shared expert always runs alongside the selected ones.",
        "Teams doing defensive security, developers running coding agents, and researchers who need to measure refusal behaviour directly instead of trusting a vendor's description.",
