      "textes": [
        "How to Generate AI Videos in Claude With the Higgsfield MCP Connector (2026)",
        "Higgsfield's MCP connector brings video, image and audio models into Claude chat.",
        "Add the connector once with the MCP URL, sign in to Higgsfield, then describe the clip you want in a chat. Claude picks a model and settings, writes the prompt, runs the generation and hands back the clip. According to Higgsfield, it shows the credit cost and waits for your go-ahead before running. Results land in the conversation and in History and Assets on higgsfield.ai, so you can reuse them as references. You can also name a model in the prompt, run the same brief across Kling and Seedance, or go from an uploaded image to video. No API key, and Claude never sees your Higgsfield password.",
        "Generation now happens inside the chat: Claude turns a plain-language brief into generation settings, and in the publisher's own test it broke a one-paragraph brief into four shots before running anything. The credit cost is surfaced for approval, not hidden. The connector sits alongside other ways in — ChatGPT plugin, Cursor Marketplace, Higgsfield CLI for coding agents.",
        "Text-to-video, image-to-video through an upload window, multi-model comparisons, vertical or upscaled versions of a finished clip, and Marketing Studio or Ad Multiplier work — all without leaving the conversation.",
        "People already working in Claude who want video generation without a second tab, including teams where an Owner or Primary Owner has to enable connectors first.",
        "Unlimited models and free generations don't work through the connector — those stay on higgsfield.ai, and images attached to the chat can't be used.",
        "No API key, just the MCP URL",
        "Cost shown before it runs",
        "Clips saved to History and Assets"
      ]
