        "Build specialized multimodal models with LFM3",
        "LiquidAI's LFM3 puts text, vision, audio and decision models on one 2B backbone",
        "Everything stays small enough to fine-tune on one GPU and deploy where the app lives. Six models in the 2B class branch from LFM3-1.7B-Base: text, vision, audio, omni and two decision models that answer a batch of questions in a single pass with calibrated probabilities. The text model runs in roughly 1 GB at 4-bit and takes long contexts. The pitch is specialization: short fine-tunes on your own data, vocabulary and tools, with notebooks covering SFT, DPO, GRPO and CPT across modalities.",
        "A redesigned backbone: tri-hybrid layers mixing gated convolutions with sliding-window and global attention, head-wise gating, partial RoPE and sandwich norm. Vision and audio encoders are new and built in-house, and LiquidCodec is a new audio tokenizer. The vision model now accepts video, and the family gains its first omni model.",
        "Builders who want small models they can own: agent developers on edge devices, robotics teams, and anyone with a narrow domain task worth a short fine-tune.",
