        "Improvements to agent-generated vector illustrations and icons",
        "Figma's agent now draws cleaner vector icons and illustrations",
        "The Figma agent's vector output is built to iterate on rather than flatten. Layers come grouped into independent parts, so you can tweak one element without rebuilding the whole drawing. Hand the agent an existing illustration as a style reference and it can spin up extra components or a set of icons that fit your look. Line work uses real strokes, so weight and end caps stay adjustable. And because the layer structure is clean, the same vectors are ready for Figma Motion when you want them animated.",
        "Agent output switches from hard-to-edit vector to grouped, stroke-based layers you can keep working with.",
