      "accroche": {
        "texte": "Claude Code v2.1.309: sandbox fixes, but not every Bash check is airtight",
        "passages": [
          "Fixed sandboxed Bash commands on macOS and Linux",
          "Bash permission check"
        ]
      },
      "description": {
        "texte": "This release mostly closes gaps where guardrails could be bypassed. In the sandbox, shell startup files no longer run outside it before each command, denyWrite patterns now apply at a path's real location behind a symlink, and sandboxed commands or auto-accepted edits can no longer modify the MCP config file passed with --mcp-config. Bash permission checks are more careful: a redirect to a path covered by an Edit(path) deny rule is blocked, compound commands that change directory before git now prompt like a plain cd when the cd is wrapped or prefixed, and PowerShell checks stop auto-approving Set-Location or cd commands outside the current directory. Worktree-isolated sessions reject locale-prefixed and zsh arithmetic commands the isolation guard should refuse. Smaller comforts too: an oversized nested CLAUDE.md loads only its start instead of triggering repeated compaction, and long tool outputs are no longer cut through an emoji, which left transcripts that jq could not parse.",
        "passages": [
          "running the shell's startup files outside the sandbox",
          "when the pattern's folder is reached through a symlink",
          "the MCP config file passed with --mcp-config",
          "an Edit(path) deny rule not blocking a Bash redirect",
          "the cd is wrapped or prefixed",
          "sessions compacting repeatedly after reading files under a very large nested CLAUDE.md",
          "cut through an emoji, leaving session transcripts that jq could not parse"
        ]
      },
      "nouveaute": {
        "texte": "The fixes target how rules are actually enforced: symlinks, redirects, subshells, locale prefixes, extra arguments. The hardening covers cases where the guard let through a command equivalent to one it would not allow.",
        "passages": [
          "a path's real location",
          "in some commands that also held a subshell",
          "some locale-prefixed commands"
        ]
      },
      "ce_que_ca_permet": {
        "texte": "Rely on deny rules and the sandbox for awkward cases: symlinked paths, redirects, wrapped cd commands, prefixed zsh commands. In parallel, fewer broken transcripts, and a nested CLAUDE.md over the limit no longer causes repeated compaction since it loads only its start.",
        "passages": [
          "a nested CLAUDE.md over the size limit now loads only its start",
          "the isolation guard should refuse"
        ]
      },
      "pour_qui": null,
      "limites_connues": null,
      "reperes": [
        {
          "texte": "Sandbox: startup files held inside",
          "passages": [
            "outside the sandbox"
          ]
        },
        {
          "texte": "denyWrite follows the real path",
          "passages": [
            "a path's real location"
          ]
        },
        {
          "texte": "Redirect stopped by Edit(path) deny",
          "passages": [
            "not blocking a Bash redirect"
          ]
        }
      ],
