      "kind": "annonce",
      "titre": "CodeQL 2.27.3 adds Python 3.15 features and JSON data extensions",
      "titre_media": "CodeQL",
      "date_annonce": "2026-11-03T14:56:03.000Z",
      "categories": [
        "sécurité",
        "outil de développement"
      ],
      "accroche": {
        "texte": "CodeQL 2.27.3 ships: Python 3.15 features, JSON data extensions, wider language coverage",
        "passages": [
          "CodeQL 2.27.3 adds Python 3.15 features and JSON data extensions"
        ]
      },
      "description": {
        "texte": "Release 2.27.3 of the analysis engine behind code scanning is out. It reads Python 3.15 syntax, takes JSON for data extensions, and handles C23 bit-precise integers. Query accuracy gets attention across several languages, and there is a new threat model for LLM-generated data that you have to switch on yourself. Anyone using code scanning on github.com gets it without doing anything.",
        "passages": [
          "CodeQL is the static analysis engine behind GitHub code scanning",
          "We’ve recently released CodeQL 2.27.3",
          "The Python extractor now supports Python 3.15 syntax",
          "We’ve added support for C23 bit-precise integers (_BitInt(N))",
          "an opt-in ai threat model for LLM-generated data",
          "Every new version of CodeQL is automatically deployed to users of GitHub code scanning on github.com"
        ]
      },
      "nouveaute": {
        "texte": "The Python side now copes with 3.15 syntax: unary plus inside match literal patterns, Unicode 17 identifiers, and the new frozendict and sentinel builtins with data flow modeling for frozendict construction. Data extension files can be JSON laid out like the YAML ones, and Java-style comments work there too; only .json files go down the JSON path while the rest stay YAML.",
        "passages": [
          "The Python extractor now supports Python 3.15 syntax, including unary plus in match literal patterns and Unicode 17 identifiers",
          "We’ve added support for the new frozendict and sentinel builtins introduced in Python 3.15, including data flow modeling for frozendict construction",
          "Data extension files now support JSON syntax, using the same structure as YAML data extensions",
          "CodeQL parses files with the .json extension as JSON and continues to parse all other files as YAML"
        ]
      },
      "ce_que_ca_permet": {
        "texte": "Under the ai threat model you plug in your own sources through data extensions, since nothing comes modelled out of the box. C# follows data flow through positional patterns, C/C++ gets flow summaries for BlazingMQ message classes and their iterators, Ruby counts Grape::API request sub-accessors as remote flow sources, and private registry setups forward proxy and certificate variables to the NuGet CLI.",
        "passages": [
          "It doesn’t include any built-in source models, so you can define your own sources with data extensions",
          "We’ve added support for data flow through positional patterns",
          "We’ve added flow summaries for the BlazingMQ BloombergLP::bmqa::Message and MessageProperties classes and their iterators",
          "treats Grape::API request sub-accessors as remote flow sources",
          "passes the required proxy and certificate environment variables to the NuGet CLI"
        ]
      },
      "pour_qui": {
        "texte": "Teams running code scanning on github.com, and anyone writing custom queries or data extensions who wants the new syntax and flow modeling without waiting.",
        "passages": [
          "If you use an older version of GHES, you can manually upgrade your CodeQL version",
          "If your custom queries rely on specific CFG nodes, edges, or basic block boundaries, you may need to update them"
        ]
      },
      "limites_connues": {
        "texte": "Custom GitHub Actions queries that rely on specific CFG nodes, edges or basic block boundaries may need updating, since the legacy Completion classes are gone.",
        "passages": [
          "The GitHub Actions control flow graph (CFG) now uses the shared CFG library",
          "We’ve removed the legacy Completion classes"
        ]
      },
      "reperes": [
        {
          "texte": "Python 3.15 syntax support",
          "passages": [
            "The Python extractor now supports Python 3.15 syntax"
          ]
        },
        {
          "texte": "JSON data extension files",
          "passages": [
            "Data extension files now support JSON syntax"
          ]
        },
        {
          "texte": "Opt-in ai threat model",
          "passages": [
            "We’ve added an opt-in ai threat model"
          ]
        }
      ],
